<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. wheat major net sales activity in the week ended Oct 3 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:    1996/97		   1997/98</p>
<p> Pakistan     120,200		    Nil</p>
<p> Colombia	29,500</p>
<p> Turkey	  28,000</p>
<p> Nigeria	 25,500</p>
<p> Bangladesh    25,000</p>
<p> Unknown	-45,900</p>
<p>Net sales of 296,200 tonnes were 50 percent below the previous week and 40 percent below the four-week average.</p>
<p>Exports of 695,000 tonnes were 27 percent below the week earlier, and 16 percent lower than the four-week average.</p>
<p>    Primary Export Destinations: Egypt (107,500), Pakistan (94,500), Japan (61,800),</p>
<p>Nigeria (52,600), Philippines (36,800) and South Korea (35,300)</p>
</text>
